25D — Generate simultaneous competing hospital traffic

Now we'll deliberately create competing demand.

First make sure old iperf processes aren't running:

h1 pkill iperf
h2 pkill iperf
h3 pkill iperf
h4 pkill iperf

Start three UDP servers on different ports at h4:

h4 iperf -s -u -p 5001 &
h4 iperf -s -u -p 5002 &
h4 iperf -s -u -p 5003 &

Generate three simultaneous flows:

h1 iperf -c 10.0.0.4 -u -p 5001 -b 3M -t 30 &
h2 iperf -c 10.0.0.4 -u -p 5002 -b 3M -t 30 &
h3 iperf -c 10.0.0.4 -u -p 5003 -b 3M -t 30 &

We now have:

h1 → h4    3 Mbps
h2 → h4    3 Mbps
h3 → h4    3 Mbps
-------------------
Offered demand ≈ 9 Mbps

Do not accidentally run any client twice like in Step 24.

While those are running:

h3 ping -c 15 -i 0.2 10.0.0.4

This represents our controlled critical-flow latency observation for this test.

